From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iwanicki92 <iwanicki92@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 15:45:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] slaunch: mark the EFI boot services finished in dl_entry

On the EFI boot path the OS exits the boot services and then calls
dl_entry through the SLRT's dl_handler. GRUB still has grub_efi_is_finished
clear at that point, so with "set debug=slaunch" the grub_dprintf calls on
the launch path (the PSP lookup, the TMR setup) write to the EFI console
through ConOut, whose firmware code may already be gone. The machine then
hangs or takes an exception (#UD or #DB at a low RIP) before SKINIT.

Set grub_efi_is_finished when entering dl_entry on the EFI path, as GRUB
does when it exits the boot services itself. The EFI console then drops
the output, and the serial terminal still prints it.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: iwanicki92 <iwanicki92@gmail.com>
---
 grub-core/loader/slaunch/dlstub.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/grub-core/loader/slaunch/dlstub.c b/grub-core/loader/slaunch/dlstub.c
index dbbd46f7d..f7f754b3e 100644
--- a/grub-core/loader/slaunch/dlstub.c
+++ b/grub-core/loader/slaunch/dlstub.c
@@ -33,6 +33,10 @@
 #include <grub/i386/txt.h>
 #include <grub/i386/skinit.h>
 
+#ifdef GRUB_MACHINE_EFI
+#include <grub/efi/efi.h>
+#endif
+
 GRUB_MOD_LICENSE ("GPLv3+");
 
 extern void dl_trampoline(grub_uint32_t dce_base, grub_uint32_t dce_size, grub_uint32_t platform);
@@ -44,6 +48,15 @@ void dl_entry (grub_uint64_t dl_ctx)
   struct grub_relocator32_state state = {0};
   grub_err_t err;
 
+#ifdef GRUB_MACHINE_EFI
+  /*
+   * On the EFI boot path the OS calls here after it has exited the boot
+   * services, so the EFI console and memory services must not be used.
+   */
+  if (slparams->boot_type == GRUB_SL_BOOT_TYPE_EFI)
+    grub_efi_is_finished = 1;
+#endif
+
   state.edi = slparams->platform_type;
 
   /* This is done on both Intel and AMD platforms */
-- 
2.43.0

